  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday night through next Wednesday)\nIssued at 111 PM CST Wed Nov 25 2026\n\nA fairly dry pattern should continue for this weekend through early \nnext week. Temperatures will warm up Friday and Saturday as the cold \nsurface high pressure moves eastward to the Gulf coast and warm \nsoutherly return flow resumes. High temperatures look to climb into \nthe 60s and 70s while low temperatures will be in the upper 30s to \nmid 40s. Another upper-level system will move out of the Rockies on \nSaturday which will make surface winds stronger that afternoon.  At \nthis point, winds should be from the southwest at 15-20 MPH with \ngusts near 30 in the afternoon.  Global models currently show the \naforementioned system pushing a stronger cold front into Texas late \nSaturday night through Sunday morning.  Winds behind the front on \nSunday morning also look to be breezy from the north at 15-20 MPH. \nOtherwise, precipitation chances are low (<10%) with this front but \nhigh temperatures should be held down to the mid 50s during the day \non Sunday due to cold advection.  Temperatures should recover rather \nquickly into the 60s and 70s for early next week as southerly flow \nresumes.",
